# vicebery.github.io

The published static files live at the repository root for GitHub Pages.

The Astro source is in [`site/`](site/). To update the site locally:

1. Install dependencies in `site/`.
2. Run `npm run build`.
3. Copy `site/dist/` to the repository root and commit the resulting static files.

The earlier static output remains at the repository root, so existing URLs stay available during the migration. `site/public/` contains only assets required by the Astro source.
